{
  "description": "An executed OP_CODESEPARATOR together with a trailing UNDECODABLE PUSH: where the separator rule meets the node's SerializeScriptCode, which declares size() - nCodeSeparators and writes only the bytes up to the failed GetOp.",
  "whyThisExists": "test/data/sighash-scriptcode-tail.json, our other node-measured sighash corpus, contains ZERO rows whose script holds a 0xab byte. Before these rows no separator-bearing scriptCode had ever been judged by a node for this library; coverage rested on an equivalence argument plus our own model.",
  "provenance": {
    "rowsAuthoredBy": "this project - the transaction, scripts and hash types were chosen here to exercise the interaction, with no expected values",
    "rowsMd5": "b2dc044a7b18fd7e59bc995febd9b154",
    "expectedValuesFrom": "the nts frontier session, 2026-10-16T12:28:13Z, git commit 29cefc69cedff3fd3e49e93fe24374f843414b31",
    "emitters": [
      {
        "witness": "compiled bitcoin-sv v1.2.3 reference, its own CTransactionSignatureSerializer",
        "binarySha256": "4813b1dd53fb3eb2d18e110feadc52311aa235f2eb3ec3e52bbc617404614093"
      },
      {
        "witness": "newsatoshi SmartSats node, an independent Rust implementation",
        "binarySha256": "5dc792db4db969641b839676a911eb587e94b98f0eef537dfde03abf80448e44"
      }
    ],
    "eachEmitterDriftChecked": "every row carried xcheck='match', meaning that emitter's copy of the serializer reproduced its OWN parent implementation's authoritative digest function (SignatureHash / script::sighash::signature_hash). All 48 rows matched in both.",
    "witnessCaveat": "The two emitters' output files are byte-identical to each other. For a deterministic function emitted in one format that is what agreement looks like, so it is not evidence of copying - but it does mean the two-witness claim rests on the provenance sidecars and the distinct binary hashes above, not on the column bytes. The peer's own wording: 'two binaries whose outputs coincide, both run by the same peer.' Same operator, same machine, same timestamp.",
    "independentlyJoined": "Joined here against a FRESH run of this library over the same rows, not against a stored column: 96 comparisons (48 rows x 2 emitters), 0 preimage differences, 0 digest differences, and every row's digest confirmed to be sha256d of its own preimage.",
    "rechecked": "the test reading this file re-derives each digest as sha256d of the preimage beside it, so a corrupted row fails rather than passing silently"
  },
  "rule": "scriptCode is the byte suffix at codeSepEnd. The original algorithm then declares len(suffix) - separators_reached_by_the_walk and writes the walked bytes with separators excised, stopping where GetOp first failed - so the field can declare more bytes than it carries. BIP-143 writes the suffix verbatim.",
  "digestOrder": "forward, i.e. sha256d(preimage) unreversed",
